Title: THE LONG WAY HOME
Author: SCS Sample

INT. GREYHOUND BUS - NIGHT

Rows of sleeping passengers. A single reading light burns over MARA VANCE, 30s, wire-rimmed glasses, a road atlas open on her lap. She traces a highway with one finger.

Across the aisle, an old man watches her. This is DELL, 70s, paper-thin, holding a shoebox tied with string.

DELL
You won't find it on that map.

MARA
(not looking up)
Find what?

DELL
Whatever it is you keep looking for. Been watching you trace that same road since Amarillo.

Mara closes the atlas. Looks at him for the first time.

MARA
It's a shortcut.

DELL
(smiling)
No such thing, sweetheart. There's just the long way, and the way you regret.

CLOSE ON THE SHOEBOX

The string is knotted twice. A name is written on the lid in faded pencil: ROSALIND.

[[Beat: Mara decides to engage. This is where the story actually starts.]]

MARA
What's in the box?

DELL
The long way.

CUT TO:

EXT. REST STOP - PARKING LOT - NIGHT

The bus idles under sodium lights. Mara stands alone, breath fogging. Through the window, Dell's seat is empty.

The shoebox sits on the bench beside her.

MARA
(quietly)
Hey. Hey!

She spins around. The lot is empty. Somewhere out past the lights, a truck door slams.

INT. GREYHOUND BUS - MOVING - LATER

Mara back in her seat, shoebox on her lap. She picks at the knot. Stops. Ties her finger into the string instead, like she's afraid of it.

The reading light flickers off.

FADE OUT.
